  "name": "DoctoBERT / FineMed pipeline",
  "alternateName": [
    "FineMed data-curation pipeline"
  ],
  "description": "Reproducible data-curation and pretraining pipeline behind DoctoBERT and the FineMed corpus, from Doctolib Lab. Scores medical documents across three axes — subdomain, educational quality, and medical-term density — then uses an LLM to rephrase documents into denser variants, and pretrains encoders on the result (built on the ModernBERT codebase). Includes components for training medical entity extractors (GLiNER), subdomain and educational-quality classifiers, and generating synthetic clinical documents. Python and Shell. Note: the repository has no LICENSE file at review time, so code reuse terms are unstated even though the released models (Apache-2.0) and data (ODC-BY-1.0 / CC-BY-SA-4.0) are licensed.",
