  "mach:judgement": "Caution",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The reproducible pipeline that produced DoctoBERT and FineMed — a genuinely useful, current (June 2026) reference for medical-encoder data curation: multi-axis document scoring, LLM rephrasing, and ModernBERT-based pretraining, with a paper documenting the method. It is marked Caution, not Assess, for one decisive reason: the repository has no LICENSE file at review time, and GitHub displays no licence. Without a licence, default copyright applies — there is no grant to use, modify, or redistribute the code, regardless of the permissively licensed models and data it produces. Teams can read it as a reference, but cannot safely reuse or build on the code until the authors add a licence. The companion model (doctobert, Apache-2.0) and dataset (finemed, ODC-BY-1.0 / CC-BY-SA-4.0) are properly licensed and cataloged separately. Re-verify on next review; if a permissive LICENSE is added, this should be re-rated to Assess.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-24",
  "schema:comment": "No LICENSE file in github.com/doctolib-lab/doctobert as of 2026-06-24 (GitHub shows no licence; /blob/main/LICENSE is 404). Code reuse terms unstated. Re-verify next review; if a LICENSE is added set license + licenseVerified accordingly and reconsider judgement.",
